<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nero Claudius Drusus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">38–9 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Drusus the Elder, Drusus Germanicus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> Drusus, known as Drusus the Elder, was a Roman general, stepson of the emperor Augustus and younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a>. From 12 to 9 BCE he led campaigns across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> against the Sugambri, Chatti, Cherusci and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanic-peoples">Germanic peoples</a>, reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, and he dug a canal and sailed along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> coast. He died in 9 BCE after a fall from his horse and was given the posthumous title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nero-claudius-drusus.jpg" alt="Nero Claudius Drusus" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Siren-Com · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drusus_l%27ancien_Rome_augGP2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
